<h2 class="font-headline-md text-headline-md text-primary mb-4">Types of Pus in Gums (Gumboils)</h2>
</div>
<div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-8">
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-secondary mb-4 icon-fill-1">healing</span><h3 class="font-headline-sm text-xl text-primary mb-3">Acute Apical Abscess (Gumboil)</h3><p class="text-on-surface-variant">A pus-filled swelling on the gum at the apex (tip) of a tooth root. Caused by bacterial infection of the tooth pulp reaching the root tip. The tooth is sensitive to touch and temperature. This is the most common cause of visible pus on gums. <a href="dental-abscess-treatment-hyderabad.php" class="text-secondary underline hover:text-primary">Dental abscess treatment</a> covers this in detail.</p></div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-secondary mb-4 icon-fill-1">healing</span><h3 class="font-headline-sm text-xl text-primary mb-3">Periodontal Abscess (Gum Pocket Pus)</h3><p class="text-on-surface-variant">Pus discharging from an existing periodontal (gum) pocket. The gum swells acutely, is very tender, and may have spontaneous pus discharge. Associated with advanced gum disease and deep pocket depths. See our <a href="gum-infection-treatment-hyderabad.php" class="text-secondary underline hover:text-primary">gum infection treatment</a> page.</p></div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-secondary mb-4 icon-fill-1">healing</span><h3 class="font-headline-sm text-xl text-primary mb-3">Pericoronitis Pus</h3><p class="text-on-surface-variant">Pus and swelling from infection under the gum flap of a partially erupted tooth — typically a lower wisdom tooth. The gum flap traps food and bacteria, causing acute inflammation with pus discharge and difficulty swallowing.</p></div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-secondary mb-4 icon-fill-1">healing</span><h3 class="font-headline-sm text-xl text-primary mb-3">Necrotizing Ulcerative Gingivitis (NUG)</h3><p class="text-on-surface-variant">A painful, rapidly destructive gum infection with crater-like ulcers between teeth and gray foul-smelling tissue. Significant pus production and bleeding from gums. Requires urgent debridement and antibiotics. <a href="bacterial-mouth-infection-treatment-hyderabad.php" class="text-secondary underline hover:text-primary">Bacterial mouth infection</a> covers this.</p></div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-surface-variant"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-secondary mb-4 icon-fill-1">healing</span><h3 class="font-headline-sm text-xl text-primary mb-3">Post-Extraction Alveolar Osteitis</h3><p class="text-on-surface-variant">A dry socket with secondary infection — pus accumulates in the empty tooth socket after extraction. Causes severe pain, bad breath, and may have pus discharge. Requires socket irrigation and medicated dressing. <a href="painful-gum-swelling-treatment-hyderabad.php" class="text-secondary underline hover:text-primary">Painful gum swelling</a> covers this condition.</p></div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-secondary mb-4 icon-fill-1">healing</span><h3 class="font-headline-sm text-xl text-primary mb-3">Mucogingival Abscess</h3><p class="text-on-surface-variant">A localized pus collection in the gum tissue that is not directly associated with a tooth root. Often arises from a blocked mucous gland duct or a foreign body in the gum. Treated by incision and drainage.</p></div>
</div>
