<ul class="space-y-6">
<li><h4 class="font-semibold text-primary mb-2">Incision and Drainage</h4><p class="text-on-surface-variant text-sm">A small incision made in the gumboil to drain the pus. Provides immediate pain relief. A small drainage stent may be placed to allow continued drainage for 24–48 hours.</p></li>
<li><h4 class="font-semibold text-primary mb-2">Antibiotic Therapy</h4><p class="text-on-surface-variant text-sm">Amoxicillin-clavulanate for most gum infections. Clindamycin for penicillin-allergic patients. Antibiotics alone are NOT the complete treatment — they must be combined with source treatment. <a href="painful-gum-swelling-treatment-hyderabad.php" class="text-secondary underline">Painful gum swelling treatment</a> covers this in detail.</p></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 md:p-12 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant">
<div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-6 pb-6 border-b border-surface-variant">
<div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-full bg-primary/10 flex items-center justify-center text-primary"><span class="material-symbols-outlined">medical_services</span></div>
<h3 class="font-headline-sm text-primary">Surgical Treatment</h3>
</div>
<ul class="space-y-6">
<li><h4 class="font-semibold text-primary mb-2">Root Canal Treatment</h4><p class="text-on-surface-variant text-sm">For a restorable tooth with a dental origin gumboil — removal of the infected dental pulp from inside the tooth and root, disinfection, and filling. Eliminates the source of the gumboil. <a href="dental-abscess-treatment-hyderabad.php" class="text-secondary underline">Dental abscess treatment</a> has full details.</p></li>
<li><h4 class="font-semibold text-primary mb-2">Tooth Extraction</h4><p class="text-on-surface-variant text-sm">For non-restorable teeth (severe bone loss or structural damage) — extraction removes the source tooth entirely. Prevents future gumboil recurrence from the same tooth.</p></li>
</ul>
